# Allowlist: exclude everything, then re-include exactly what the extension runs.
# The exclusion list this replaces shipped an untracked claim note holding a
# private home path in 0.6.9 (found 2026-10-19), because vsce packages the
# working directory and an exclusion list only covers names someone remembered.
# package.json "files" is not honoured while this file exists (vsce 3.9.2), so
# the allowlist lives here. test/vsix-contents.test.mjs asks vsce what it ships.
#
# Every dependency is build-time: package.json declares "dependencies": {} and
# esbuild bundles the extension and Claude adapters into dist/.
**
!dist/extension.js
!dist/adapters/*.mjs
!native/windows-focus-helper.exe
!README.md
!LICENSE
!THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md
!CHANGELOG.md
!images/icon.png
